{"screens":{"Bram Halloway":"You step out of the staves' shadow and swing wide of Tobin, who stands planted at the bend with his back to the warehouse. With your shield on your arm and your sword sheathed, you walk north up the Coast Way at a road man's pace. The forge's red spill slides off your mail, and then Gorm's yellow lantern light takes over.

Gorm turns before you are halfway there. He stays at the wagon's front wheel with the lantern raised and watches you come the way he'd watch a horse he didn't remember hitching. The carter keeps the cob's head short. You call your question up the street as you approach: men are shouting about an open shutter and an empty wagon at his door, and you ask whether the one on the bench is Oake's clerk. The cloaked figure sits back as your voice carries, and the hood turns a little toward you.

You step into the light and look up under the hood.","together":[["Bram Halloway"]],"places":{"Bram Halloway":"On the Coast Way, in Gorm's lantern light beside the wagon"},"waiting":{}}
